Use `AGENTS.md` as the source of truth for project-wide agent instructions.

Documentation map:

- `docs/README.md` - documentation index and update rules.
- `docs/specs/assignment-1-rest-web-demo.md` - REST/web/Android demo spec.
- `docs/specs/assignment-2-response-control.md` - response-control assignment spec.
- `docs/agent-notes/llm-demo-assignment-2.md` - implementation decisions, provider notes, debugging workflow, and guardrails.

When editing `llm_demo`, read the assignment 2 spec and agent notes first if the change touches response-control behavior.

Cursor-specific rule: this file is always attached but intentionally short. Do not duplicate long specs or debug notes here; update the canonical docs instead.

Key guardrails:

- Keep LLM calls as explicit REST via `httpx.post`.
- Keep exactly three modes: `none`, `api`, `system`.
- Keep the same `user` prompt in every mode.
- Do not auto-fallback on OpenRouter `response_format` errors.
